        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#human_reference_atlas"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Frequently used when describing the developing nervous system in zebrafish. A catecholaminergic neuron expresses tyrosine hydroxylase (TH), tyrosine hydroxylase 2 (TH2), aromatic amino acid decarboxylase (AADC), dopamine b-hydroxylase (DBH), and phenylethanolamine-N-methyl transferase (PEMT), which are enzymes necessary for catecholamine synthesis.</rdfs:comment>
