        <obo:IAO_0000115>Major subdivision of an organism that protrudes from the body[DOS, CARO].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>An appendage is an external body part, or natural prolongation, that protrudes from an organism&apos;s body, such as a vertebrate&apos;s limbs[BILA][BILA:0000018].</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>Organ or organ part that is attached to the body of an organism. For example a limb[GO, modified][GO:0048736].</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000007>appendicular</obo:UBPROP_0000007>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>this is currently a subtype of organism subdivision - which would exclude feathers</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
