        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001645"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000008"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>the ophthalmic usually usually merges with the other two. In some vertebrates, the ophthalmic emerges from the brain separately[Kardong] The trigeminal nerve has 3 branches in mammals - similar branches are present in nonmammalian vertebrates, but in some a separate profundus nerve that corresponds to opthalmic branch in mammls</owl:annotatedTarget>
