        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="genid2377"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="genid2379"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The large, irregular bone located at the base and side of the skull; consists of three parts at birth: squamous, tympanic, and petrous.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000233 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/3791</obo:IAO_0000233>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>In many mammals, as in humans, the petrosal, ectotympanic and squamosal bones synostose to form the temporal bone + styloid process</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>fusion of squamosal + angular (tympanic annulus) [derm.] + petrosal (prootic + opisthotic)</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000010>The temporal bone consists of four parts: * Squama temporalis * Mastoid portion * Petrous portion (Petrosal ridge) * Tympanic part[WP].</obo:UBPROP_0000010>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>Note the Temporal bone is not explicitly categorized to a part of the cranium in FMA</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA:6035</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:17682</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
