    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002140 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002140">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0011214"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002473"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000108"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Cholinergic cell group that is located ventral to the brachium of the inferior colliculus (in rat) and has reciprocal connectivity with the superior colliculus (Adapted from Paxinos, The rat central nervous system, 2nd ed, 1995, pg 865.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>Nucleus isthmi is present in the isthmus in most vertebrates. It is called the parabigeminal nucleus in mammals (reference 1); In sum, our results show that the origin of neurons of some tegmental hindbrain nuclei, namely, nucleus isthmi/superior reticular nucleus and secondary gustatory/viscerosensory nucleus is in the URL (upper rhombic lip), and that the temporal order of cell types produced by the URL and their developmental program are conserved among vertebrate species (reference 2).[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>in MA this is part of the tegmentum/brainstem</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:PBG</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BIRNLEX:1007</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BM:PBG</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DHBA:12312</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
