            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An organ that houses olfactory neurons and is responsible for the sense of smell. Examples include the vertebrate nose and the Drosophila dorsal organ.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>An olfactory organ overlaps with the olfactory system, because some parts of the nose (e.g. nasal skeleton) are parts of the skeletal system, which is spatially disjoint</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>fma general anatomical term. xao has no subtypes (but Johnstons organ develops from this). An olfactory organ overlaps with the olfactory system, because some parts of the nose (e.g. nasal skeleton) are parts of the skeletal system, which is spatially disjoint</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>AAO:0010180</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BTO:0001772</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
