        <owl:annotatedTarget>The dorsal cochlear nucleus (DCN, also known as the &apos;tuberculum acousticum&apos;), is a cortex-like structure on the dorso-lateral surface of the brainstem. Along with the ventral cochlear nucleus, it forms the cochlear nucleus, where all auditory nerve fibers from the cochlea form their first synapses. [WP,unvetted].</owl:annotatedTarget>
