        <obo:IAO_0000115>The Medial parabrachial nucleus is a nucleus of the pons which constitutes part of the pneumotaxic center. It gets its name from its location relative to the superior cerebellar peduncles, which is also known as the &apos;brachia conjunctiva&apos;. [WP,unvetted].</obo:IAO_0000115>
