            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="genid9575"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The central area of the two limbs of a horseshoe-shaped mesenchymal swelling that lie medial to the olfactory placode or pit in the future nasal region of the embryo; it joins with the ipsilateral maxillary prominence in the formation of half of the upper jaw, and the nasal tip and philtrum of the upper lip develop from it.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000011>Fusion of right and left medial nasal processes forms a primary palate rostrally and the nasal septum caudally. The incisive bone, including upper incisor teeth and the rostral up- per lip, are derived from the primary palate. The nasal septum consists of bone, cartilage, and a patch of soft tissue membrane that separates right &amp; left halves of the nasal cavity.</obo:UBPROP_0000011>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA2:0001076</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA:4792</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:16808</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:295858</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:308877001</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VHOG:0000804</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Medial_nasal_prominence</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>medial nasal process</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>medial-nasal process</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>prominentia nasalis medialis</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>medial nasal swelling</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>nasomedial prominence</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0004068</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#pheno_slim"/>
