        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="genid9649"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The uvula (uvular lobe) forms a considerable portion of the inferior vermis; it is separated on either side from the tonsil by the sulcus valleculC&amp;, at the bottom of which it is connected to the tonsil by a ridge of gray matter, indented on its surface by shallow furrows, and hence called the furrowed band.</obo:IAO_0000115>
