    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004170 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004170">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0007838"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The band of nerve fibers which cross the midline of the spinal cord ventral to the central canal and posterior grey commissure[MP]. The anterior (or ventral) white commissure, also known as the alba anterior medullae spinalis, is a bundle of nerve fibers which cross the midline of the spinal cord just anterior to the gray commissure. A N4 fibers and C fibers carrying pain sensation in the spinothalamic tract contribute to this commissure, as do fibers of the anterior corticospinal tract, which carry motor signals from the primary motor cortex[WP].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:vc</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
