        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004003"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A lobule comprising the greater part of the hemisphere of the cerebellum; its superior and inferior surfaces are separated by the horizontal fissure into major parts known as crus I (superior semilunar lobule) and crus II (inferior semilunar lobule).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002171 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001063"/>
        <obo:RO_0002171 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005347"/>
        <obo:RO_0002171 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005349"/>
        <obo:RO_0002171 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005350"/>
        <obo:RO_0002171 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005351"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>MP says the ansiform lobule not present in humans; however, FMA seems to have this, as well as two subclasses, so for now we group based on synonymy from multiple sources</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:AN</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:An</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
