        <owl:annotatedTarget>The term dorsal striatum refers to a composite structure of the endbrain that is defined in the striatopallidal system by connectivity and neurochemical staining. It includes most of the striatum ( Heimer-1995 ). The boundary between this structure and the ventral striatum is indistinct in sections stained for Nissl substance.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:source>neuronames:2340</oboInOwl:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
