    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0015800 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0015800">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0016536"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0016555"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002264"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002665"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A continuation ventrally of the supracallosal gyrus beyond the rostrum of the corpus callosum. It is demonstrated histologically by Nissl stain. In the human ( Anthoney-1994 ) and the macaque ( Paxinos-2004 ) it lies on the rostral surface of the lamina terminalis and is considered identical to or part of the paraterminal gyrus. In the rat ( Swanson-1998 ) and the mouse ( Paxinos-2001 ) it is located similarly in relation to the supracallosal gyrus, however, it is a more prominent layered structure that extends rostrally on the medial surface overlying the anterior olfactory nucleus. It is considered part of the olfactory areas (rodent) of the cerebral cortex. In rodents it consists of two parts, the dorsal tenia tecta and the ventral tenia tecta. Note that some authors use the term &apos;tenia tecta&apos; or &apos;taenia tecta&apos; as a synonym for the lateral longitudinal stria ( Riley-1943 ).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BTO:0003738</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DHBA:10305</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DMBA:16154</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:35847</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MA:0003150</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MBA:589</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NLX:144479</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>neuronames:1870</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>taenia tecta</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>taenia tectum</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>taenia tecta</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>tenia tecta</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>tenia tectum</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0015800</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>taenia tectum of brain</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>taenia tectum of brain</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0015800"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A continuation ventrally of the supracallosal gyrus beyond the rostrum of the corpus callosum. It is demonstrated histologically by Nissl stain. In the human ( Anthoney-1994 ) and the macaque ( Paxinos-2004 ) it lies on the rostral surface of the lamina terminalis and is considered identical to or part of the paraterminal gyrus. In the rat ( Swanson-1998 ) and the mouse ( Paxinos-2001 ) it is located similarly in relation to the supracallosal gyrus, however, it is a more prominent layered structure that extends rostrally on the medial surface overlying the anterior olfactory nucleus. It is considered part of the olfactory areas (rodent) of the cerebral cortex. In rodents it consists of two parts, the dorsal tenia tecta and the ventral tenia tecta. Note that some authors use the term &apos;tenia tecta&apos; or &apos;taenia tecta&apos; as a synonym for the lateral longitudinal stria ( Riley-1943 ).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>neuronames:1870</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0015800"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>taenia tecta</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MA:0003150</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
