            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Frontal lobe is the anterior-most of five lobes of the cerebral hemisphere. It is bounded by the central sulcus on its posterior border and by the longitudinal cerebral fissure on its medial border.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Many species don&apos;t have lobes but they do have frontal cortex. Lobe isn&apos;t a really well defined term though</obo:IAO_0000116>
